  "instruction": "Open VSCode with ~/projects/python-hypothesis. Set up property-based testing with Hypothesis: (1) Install hypothesis and pytest. (2) In src/sorting.py there are three sort implementations: bubble_sort(lst), merge_sort(lst), and quick_sort(lst). Create tests/test_sorting_properties.py with Hypothesis property tests: (a) given any list of integers, all three implementations return the same result as Python's sorted(); (b) given any list, the output length equals input length; (c) given any list, the output is sorted (each element <= next). Use @given(st.lists(st.integers())) decorator. (3) In src/string_utils.py there is a parse_date(s) function — write property tests that verify the round-trip: format_date(parse_date(s)) == s for valid date strings. (4) Add a pytest.ini with hypothesis profile settings. Create a .vscode/tasks.json 'Property Tests' task.",
